# Trivy ignore file — read by aquasecurity/trivy-action (image + fs scans) by
# default. Every entry here is a SECURITY FINDING WE HAVE ASSESSED AND ACCEPTED,
# with a written justification + a re-review trigger. This is NOT a place to
# silence real exposure — a permanently-red Security Gate trains everyone to
# ignore it, so we keep the gate GREEN and document each exception here instead.
# Review this file whenever the base image / npm is bumped.

# ── npm-bundled undici + brace-expansion: REMOVAL-TESTED 2026-10-01 (W10.1b) ──
# The Security Scanning run on PR #318 (run 36894639288) read the image's
# npm CLI bundle at undici 6.28.0 and brace-expansion 5.0.9 — past the
# recorded re-review triggers of the prior entries CVE-2026-12151 (undici,
# fixed 6.27.0), CVE-2026-14257 and CVE-2026-69152 (brace-expansion, fixed
# 5.0.8). Ignored entries are invisible to falsification, so all three were
# REMOVED; restore exactly a survivor if a later scan fires it.
#
# The same run found three NEWER CVEs on those same two bundled packages:
#
# ── CVE-2026-102276 / CVE-2026-102278 — brace-expansion DoS ─────────────────
# (stack exhaustion / uncontrolled recursion from crafted brace patterns)
# Affected: brace-expansion 5.0.9 BUNDLED INSIDE the npm CLI
#   (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/brace-expansion), still
#   present after the Dockerfile's `npm install -g npm@latest`.
#   Fixed in 5.0.10 / 5.0.11 (and 3.0.8 / 2.1.6 / 1.1.20).
# Assessment — EXPOSURE NIL:
#   • The APP's copies are patched: 5.0.12, 2.1.7 and 1.1.21 in
#     package-lock.json (verified every instance 2026-10-01); `npm audit`
#     (security.yml, critical/high) gates them independently of this file.
#   • npm runs at runtime only as `npm audit --json` (runScheduledJobs.ts)
#     and `npm outdated --json` (codebaseMonitor.ts) — fixed argv, no
#     glob or brace pattern from any external input reaches npm.
# Re-review trigger: drop both lines when `npm install -g npm@latest` pulls
# a bundle with brace-expansion >= 5.0.11 (re-run the container scan after
# any npm or base-image bump).
CVE-2026-102276
CVE-2026-102278

# ── CVE-2026-19534 — undici DoS via an unrequested WebSocket subprotocol ────
# Affected: undici 6.28.0 BUNDLED INSIDE the npm CLI (same bundle as above).
#   Fixed in 6.28.1 / 7.29.1 / 8.10.2.
# Assessment — EXPOSURE NIL:
#   • The APP's undici is 7.30.0 (patched) in package-lock.json, pinned by
#     the package.json `overrides`; `npm audit` gates it.
#   • The DoS needs undici to open a WebSocket to an attacker's server. The
#     two runtime npm subprocesses make plain HTTPS requests to the npm
#     registry only; neither opens a WebSocket.
# Re-review trigger: drop when the npm bundle's undici is >= 6.28.1.
CVE-2026-19534

# ── CVE-2026-69192 — ip-address parsing flaw ────────────────────────────────
# Affected: ip-address 10.2.0 BUNDLED INSIDE the npm CLI (the global
#   npm@latest the Dockerfile installs). Fixed in 10.3.1.
# Assessment — EXPOSURE NIL:
#   • The APP's ip-address is 10.7.0 (patched) in the lockfile.
#   • Reachable only through npm's registry/proxy plumbing in the two
#     runtime subprocess calls above; no attacker-controlled address strings
#     flow into them.
# Re-review trigger: clears on npm's next bundle refresh (re-run the
# container scan after any npm or base-image bump).
CVE-2026-69192

# ── CVE-2026-73566 — tar, npm-bundled copy ──────────────────────────────────
# Affected: tar 7.5.19 INSIDE the npm CLI's vendored tree. The APP's tar is
# 7.5.22 (>= the 7.5.21 fix) via the package.json override, verified in the
# lockfile. Same npm-bundle disposition as above; re-review on npm's next
# bundle refresh.
CVE-2026-73566

# ── gh-binary Go-module CVEs: REMOVAL-TESTED at GH_VERSION v2.99.0 bump ────
# (2026-09-02) The prior entries here — CVE-2026-56852/56864/56865 (x/text
# v0.38.0, x/mod v0.37.0) and GHSA-hrxh-6v49-42gf (grpc v1.81.1) — hit their
# recorded re-review trigger when GH_VERSION bumped v2.96.0 → v2.99.0, whose
# go.mod pins x/text v0.41.0 and grpc v1.83.2 (both past their fix floors)
# but x/mod v0.39.0 (our note's floor said 0.40.0). Ignored entries are
# invisible to falsification, so ALL FOUR were removed; if the next scan
# still fires any of them, restore exactly the survivors with a
# v2.99.0-dated assessment (the nil-exposure reasoning — gh is a subprocess
# API client, no module fetching, no gRPC server — still holds if needed).
#
# REMOVAL-TEST RESULT (run 33578279866, 2026-09-02): exactly ONE survivor.
# CVE-2026-56854 (x/crypto), CVE-2026-56852/x-text pair and
# GHSA-hrxh-6v49-42gf (grpc) all cleared at v2.99.0 — entries stay removed.
#
# ── CVE-2026-56864 — golang.org/x/mod v0.39.0 in the gh v2.99.0 binary ──
# Fixed in x/mod 0.40.0; gh v2.99.0 (latest) still pins 0.39.0 upstream.
# Assessment — EXPOSURE NIL (v2.99.0-dated): the vulnerability requires a
# malicious GOSUMDB serving module data during Go module fetching; gh
# performs NO Go-module fetching at runtime — it is a subprocess API client
# for api.github.com invoked by evolutionPrGenerator.ts with our own token.
# Re-review trigger: next GH_VERSION bump — drop BOTH lines when the
# release's go.mod pins x/mod >= 0.40.0.
CVE-2026-56864
# …and CVE-2026-56865 — the SECOND x/mod v0.39.0 CVE (sumdb/tlog
# transparency-log verification), surfaced by the next scan (run
# 33580880674, 2026-09-02) after 56864 was dispositioned. Same module,
# same version, same nil exposure: gh performs no Go-module fetching and
# no sumdb verification at runtime. Same re-review trigger.
CVE-2026-56865

# ── CVE-2026-97058 — sprintf-js DoS via unbounded precision specifiers ──────
# (GHSA-hp3w-g68c-fv3c) Affected: sprintf-js 1.0.3, reached in production only
#   through mammoth -> argparse 1.0.10 -> sprintf-js. No patched sprintf-js
#   exists (npm audit: "fix available: none"; Trivy status: affected).
# Assessment — EXPOSURE NIL (2026-10-06):
#   • argparse is required ONLY by mammoth's command-line entry point
#     (node_modules/mammoth/bin/mammoth). mammoth's library code (lib/),
#     which server/ai/executive.ts imports to read .docx text, never loads
#     argparse, so sprintf-js is never loaded by the server process.
#   • Even through the CLI, the format strings are argparse's own help
#     templates, never input from a user or the network.
# Re-review trigger: drop when a patched sprintf-js ships, or when mammoth
# stops depending on argparse 1.x (re-run `npm audit` after any mammoth bump).
CVE-2026-97058
